============================================================================================
(L3) SPLITTING PARAMETER: does LOW cross-E_+ => small |corr|?  (k=8 varied two-block)
============================================================================================
  config                          crossE_+ crossSchur    |corr|
  touching [0..3]+[4..7]               256         26   0.30273
  gap1     [0..3]+[5..8]               208         23   0.05766
  gap3     [0..3]+[7..10]              176         20   0.06662
  far      [0..3]+[50..53]             176         20   0.08804
  veryfar  [0..3]+[1e5..]              176         20   0.09287
  dissoc base [0,1,3,7]+far            112         14   0.01266

  CONCLUSION: separation kills cross-Schur (support-3, M>2w-2) -> cross-E_+ floors
  -> |corr| of separated multi-block stays well below the single-block consec value.
  Additive energy IS the splitting parameter: structured(consec)=max|corr|, and the
  multi-block carrier error is bounded by the within-block (single-block) value once
  cross-block additive triangles are gone.
